Changes since commit 0f556b0873c72ba1152a12fd54c3198ee039e413
====================================================================

1) DPI-aware sizing for unlabeled toggle indicators (Motif core)
   - Files:
     - lib/Xm/Display.c
     - lib/Xm/ToggleB.c
     - lib/Xm/ToggleBG.c
     - lib/Xm/XmI.h
     - lib/Xm/libXm.elist
   - What changed:
     - Added a helper that reads Xft.dpi from the X resource database
       and computes a scale factor using a 75 DPI baseline.
     - Applied the scaled default indicator size only when toggles have
       no label/pixmap and XmNindicatorSize was not explicitly set.
   - Why:
     - Unlabeled checkboxes (e.g., permission grids) were too small on
       high-DPI displays; scaling restores usable indicator size while
       preserving existing labeled widget behavior.

2) Drag-and-drop snap-back honors hotspot (Motif core)
   - Commits: 8a13af6c, 0255c389
   - Files:
     - lib/Xm/DragOverS.c
   - What changed:
     - Snap-back animation now returns the drag hotspot to the initial
       pointer location instead of returning the pixmap center.
     - Blended drag icon hotspot now honors XmNhotX/Y from the drag
       context when provided by the application.
     - Temporary debug logging removed (commit 0255c389).
   - Why:
     - Fixes incorrect return animation when applications supply a
       custom drag hotspot (e.g., clicking on the left/right of a large
       icon label caused the pixmap center to return to the click point).

